The Amiga X server of the x11r63 package (Xzz9000): who holds which part

The server's hw/amix tree comes from patch 00, Ignacio Soriano's Amiga X
server, with the package's patches 01 onwards on top.  Its parts, and the
notice that covers each:

1. The rtg/ layer and the ZZ9000 driver (hw/amix/rtg) are based on Antti
   Sokero's xrtg-amix (its rtg/ layer and VA2000 driver), MIT:

       Copyright (c) 2025-2026 Antti Sokero

2. The ZZ9000 version of that layer and driver, mfbimage.c's depth-1 image
   code, and the rest of patch 00 that is not listed under 1 or 3, MIT:

       Copyright (c) 2026 isoriano1968

3. The Z3660 and Amix changes: those patch 00 carries from amix-z3660rtg
   (the Z3660 modes, the raster-op and window copy fixes, fills and copies
   on the card's blitter, the monitor switch, the keyboard back to the
   console when the server ends), the package's patches 01 onwards, and
   zz9000screen.c, the package's own, MIT:

       Copyright (c) 2026 Jussi Alanärä

4. The input and screen framework of hw/amix (amixInit.c, amixIo.c,
   amixKbd.c, amixMouse.c, amix.h) comes from the 1987 Sun X server through
   Commodore's Amix X server and keeps the notices of the Regents of the
   University of California and of Sun Microsystems in each file; COPYRIGHT
   in this directory lists them with the rest of X11R6.3's notices.

